module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FiberCotangentIdentification.Kaehler
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Flatness.QuotientBaseChange
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Flat.DevissageQuotientBase
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# Base change of a complete dévissage along a surjection of the base

`StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Flat.DevissageQuotientBase` analyses the base change of a complete
dévissage along a ring map of the base, condition by condition, and proves the conditions whose
transport is not formal. This file supplies the remaining, formal, conditions for the base change
along a surjection `R → R/J` with `J ⊆ r` — the one Stacks 05PG's induction step *"we may replace
`A` by `A/J`"* performs — and assembles them.

## The quotient base change of a stage

The stage data is built, not taken as a parameter: the dependent fields `alpha`, `cokerEquiv` and
`fiber_bijective` of `Module.CompleteDevissage` are typed against the module structure restricted
along the base-changed `toLeft`, so the base-changed stage algebras and stage modules have to be
*defined*. They are `Aᵢ ⧸ JAᵢ`, `Bᵢ ⧸ JBᵢ` and `Mᵢ ⧸ JAᵢ·Mᵢ`, where `JC` denotes the ideal
`Ideal.map (algebraMap R C) J` generated by `J` in an `R`-algebra `C`. Unlike
`Module.CompleteDevissage.localize`, no universe is raised: a quotient of `Mᵢ` lives in the
universe of `Mᵢ`.

## Main results

The generic inputs, which are about a quotient base change and not about dévissages:

* `Stacks.Flatness.restrictScalars_map_smul_top`: the submodule `JC·M` of `M` generated by `J` is
  the submodule `JB·M` when `M` is read over a smaller algebra `B` over `R`. This is what
  identifies the kernel of `Mᵢ → Mᵢ ⧸ JAᵢ·Mᵢ` as a map of `Bᵢ`-modules.
* `Stacks.Flatness.isBaseChange_of_surjective`: a surjection of modules whose kernel is killed by
  the kernel of a surjection of the base rings exhibits the target as a base change. This is how
  `Mᵢ ⧸ JAᵢ·Mᵢ` is seen as `(Bᵢ ⧸ JBᵢ) ⊗[Bᵢ] Mᵢ`, which the fibre condition
  (`Stacks.Flatness.fiber_bijective_of_isBaseChange`) and the cokernel identification both need.
* `Stacks.Flatness.quotBaseMapₐ`: an `R`-algebra map `C → D` base changed to an `R/J`-algebra map
  `C ⧸ JC → D ⧸ JD`, with `Stacks.Flatness.quotBaseMapₐ_surjective`,
  `Stacks.Flatness.ker_quotBaseMapₐ` and `Stacks.Flatness.finitePresentation_quotBaseMapₐ` for the
  two conditions a dévissage imposes on such a map.
* `Stacks.Flatness.smooth_quotBase` and `Stacks.Flatness.geometricallyIrreducible_quotBase`: the
  two conditions on the lower algebra, which are stability under base change applied to the
  pushout square of `Stacks.FiberCotangentIdentification.isPushout_quotient` and to the cartesian
  square of `Stacks.Flatness.isPullback_SpecMap_quotient`.
* `Stacks.Flatness.finiteTypeQuotBase`, `Stacks.Flatness.finiteQuotBase` and
  `Stacks.Flatness.isPrime_map_quotient`: the three typeclass assumptions
  `Module.CompleteDevissage` makes on its data, for the base-changed data. The first two are
  universe-free, unlike `RingHom.FiniteType.isStableUnderBaseChange`, because a quotient is
  generated by the images of generators.

The assembly itself:

* `Module.CompleteDevissage.quotientBase`: a complete dévissage of `N/S/R` over a prime `r` and an
  ideal `J ⊆ r` give a complete dévissage of `(N/JN)/(S/JS)/(R/J)` over `r/J` (Stacks 05HX). The
  stage data is `Module.CompleteDevissage.quotA`, `quotB`, `quotM`, `quotToLeft`, `quotToRight`,
  `quotToA₀`, `quotMk`, `quotAlpha`, `quotCokerEquiv` and `quotInitialEquiv`.
* `Module.CompleteDevissage.isBaseChange_quotMk`, `isBaseChange_quotMkSucc` and
  `isBaseChange_quotMk₀`: each stage module's quotient *is* its base change, which is what makes
  the stage map, the cokernel identification and the original module identification the base
  changes of the originals rather than maps that have to be checked by hand.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 05HX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05HX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05HZ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05HZ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05PG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05PG)
-/

@[expose] public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory

universe u v w

namespace Stacks.Flatness

/-! ### The submodule generated by an ideal of the base -/

/-- **The submodule of `M` generated by an ideal `J` of the base does not depend on which algebra
over `R` the module is read over.** For `R → B → C` and a `C`-module `M`, the `C`-submodule
generated by `JC` is, as a `B`-submodule, the one generated by `JB`: both are the set of sums of
elements `j • m` with `j ∈ J`.

This is what identifies the kernel of `Mᵢ → Mᵢ ⧸ JAᵢ·Mᵢ`, read as a map of `Bᵢ`-modules, with
`JBᵢ·Mᵢ`. It is `Ideal.smul_restrictScalars` once `JC` is written as the ideal generated by
`JB`. -/
@[ega "0 1.0.4" "JM = (BJ)M"]
public theorem restrictScalars_map_smul_top {R B C : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing B] [CommRing C]
    [Algebra R B] [Algebra R C] [Algebra B C] [IsScalarTower R B C] {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M]
    [Module C M] [Module B M] [IsScalarTower B C M] (J : Ideal R) :
    ((Ideal.map (algebraMap R C) J) • (⊤ : Submodule C M)).restrictScalars B
      = (Ideal.map (algebraMap R B) J) • (⊤ : Submodule B M) := by
  rw [show Ideal.map (algebraMap R C) J
      = Ideal.map (algebraMap B C) (Ideal.map (algebraMap R B) J) by
        rw [Ideal.map_map, ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_eq],
    Ideal.smul_restrictScalars, Submodule.restrictScalars_top]

/-! ### A surjection with small kernel is a base change -/

/-- **A surjection of modules whose kernel is killed by the kernel of a surjection of the base
rings exhibits its target as a base change.** If `B → B'` is a surjection of rings, `M'` is a
`B'`-module and `g : M → M'` is a surjection of `B`-modules whose kernel lies inside
`ker(B → B')·M`, then `M' = B' ⊗[B] M`.

This is how `Mᵢ ⧸ JAᵢ·Mᵢ` is recognized as the base change of `Mᵢ` along `Bᵢ → Bᵢ ⧸ JBᵢ`: the
inclusion of kernels is `Stacks.Flatness.restrictScalars_map_smul_top`. Only that one inclusion is
needed; the proof is the universal property, a `B`-linear map into a `B'`-module killing
`ker(B → B')·M` automatically, and then `LinearMap.extendScalarsOfSurjective`. -/
public theorem isBaseChange_of_surjective {B B' : Type u} [CommRing B] [CommRing B']
    [Algebra B B'] (hs : Function.Surjective (algebraMap B B')) {M : Type v} [AddCommGroup M]
    [Module B M] {M' : Type w} [AddCommGroup M'] [Module B M'] [Module B' M']
    [IsScalarTower B B' M'] (g : M →ₗ[B] M') (hgs : Function.Surjective g)
    (hker : LinearMap.ker g ≤ (RingHom.ker (algebraMap B B') : Ideal B) • (⊤ : Submodule B M)) :
    IsBaseChange B' g := by
  refine IsBaseChange.of_lift_unique g fun Q _ _ _ _ h => ?_
  let : AddCommGroup Q := Module.addCommMonoidToAddCommGroup B
  have hkerle : LinearMap.ker g ≤ LinearMap.ker h :=
    hker.trans <| Submodule.smul_le.mpr fun k hk m _ => by
      rw [LinearMap.mem_ker, map_smul, ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_smul B' k (h m),
        RingHom.mem_ker.mp hk, zero_smul]
  obtain ⟨h₀, hh₀⟩ : ∃ h₀ : M' →ₗ[B'] Q, ∀ x : M, h₀ (g x) = h x := by
    let e : (M ⧸ LinearMap.ker g) ≃ₗ[B] M' := g.quotKerEquivOfSurjective hgs
    let hq : (M ⧸ LinearMap.ker g) →ₗ[B] Q := Submodule.liftQ (LinearMap.ker g) h hkerle
    have hcomp (x : M) : hq (e.symm (g x)) = h x := by
      rw [e.symm_apply_eq.mpr (LinearMap.quotKerEquivOfSurjective_apply_mk g hgs x).symm]
      exact Submodule.liftQ_apply _ _ _
    exact ⟨(hq ∘ₗ e.symm.toLinearMap).extendScalarsOfSurjective hs, hcomp⟩
  refine ⟨h₀, LinearMap.ext hh₀, fun y hy => LinearMap.ext fun m' => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨m, rfl⟩ := hgs m'
  exact (LinearMap.congr_fun hy m).trans (hh₀ m).symm

/-! ### The quotient base change of an algebra map -/

section Map

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R] (J : Ideal R) {C D : Type*} [CommRing C] [CommRing D]
  [Algebra R C] [Algebra R D]

/-- **The ideal generated by `J` is carried to the ideal generated by `J`** by any `R`-algebra
map. -/
public theorem map_map_algebraMap (f : C →ₐ[R] D) :
    Ideal.map (f : C →+* D) (Ideal.map (algebraMap R C) J) = Ideal.map (algebraMap R D) J := by
  rw [Ideal.map_map, ← AlgHom.comp_algebraMap f]

/-- **An `R`-algebra map base changed along `R → R/J`.** -/
public def quotBaseMapₐ (f : C →ₐ[R] D) :
    (C ⧸ Ideal.map (algebraMap R C) J) →ₐ[R ⧸ J] (D ⧸ Ideal.map (algebraMap R D) J) where
  __ := Ideal.quotientMap (Ideal.map (algebraMap R D) J) (f : C →+* D)
    (by rw [← map_map_algebraMap J f]; exact Ideal.le_comap_map)
  commutes' := by
    intro x
    obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective x
    change Ideal.quotientMap _ _ _ (algebraMap (R ⧸ J) (C ⧸ _) (Ideal.Quotient.mk J y)) = _
    rw [Ideal.Quotient.algebraMap_quotient_map_quotient,
      Ideal.Quotient.algebraMap_quotient_map_quotient]
    exact congrArg (Ideal.Quotient.mk _) (f.commutes y)

/-- `quotBaseMapₐ J f` sends the class of `c` to the class of `f c`. -/
@[simp]
public theorem quotBaseMapₐ_mk (f : C →ₐ[R] D) (c : C) :
    quotBaseMapₐ J f (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ c) = Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (f c) := rfl

/-- **A surjection stays surjective after the quotient base change.** -/
public theorem quotBaseMapₐ_surjective (f : C →ₐ[R] D) (hf : Function.Surjective f) :
    Function.Surjective (quotBaseMapₐ J f) := by
  intro x
  obtain ⟨d, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective x
  obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := hf d
  exact ⟨Ideal.Quotient.mk _ c, rfl⟩

/-- **The kernel of the base change of a surjection is the image of its kernel.** For a surjective
`f : C →ₐ[R] D` the ideal `JD` is `f(JC)`, so the kernel of `C ⧸ JC → D ⧸ JD` consists of the
classes of the elements `c` with `f c ∈ f(JC)`, that is of `JC ⊔ ker f`, which is the image of
`ker f`. -/
public theorem ker_quotBaseMapₐ (f : C →ₐ[R] D) (hsurj : Function.Surjective f) :
    RingHom.ker ((quotBaseMapₐ J f : _ →ₐ[R ⧸ J] _) :
        (C ⧸ Ideal.map (algebraMap R C) J) →+* (D ⧸ Ideal.map (algebraMap R D) J))
      = Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.map (algebraMap R C) J))
          (RingHom.ker (f : C →+* D)) := by
  refine le_antisymm (fun x hx => ?_) ?_
  · obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective x
    have hfc : c ∈ Ideal.comap (f : C →+* D)
        (Ideal.map (f : C →+* D) (Ideal.map (algebraMap R C) J)) := by
      rw [Ideal.mem_comap, map_map_algebraMap J f]
      exact Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mp
        (show Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (f c) = 0 from RingHom.mem_ker.mp hx)
    rw [Ideal.comap_map_of_surjective (f : C →+* D) hsurj (Ideal.map (algebraMap R C) J)] at hfc
    obtain ⟨a, ha, b, hb, hab⟩ := Submodule.mem_sup.mp hfc
    rw [← hab, map_add, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mpr ha, zero_add]
    exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ hb
  · rw [Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
    intro c hc
    rw [Ideal.mem_comap, RingHom.mem_ker]
    show Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (f c) = 0
    rw [show f c = 0 from RingHom.mem_ker.mp hc, map_zero]

/-- **A surjection of finite presentation stays of finite presentation after the quotient base
change.**

As in `Stacks.Flatness.finitePresentation_mapₐ_of_isLocalization`, this is not
`RingHom.FinitePresentation.isStableUnderBaseChange`: that holds for a ring map between types in
one universe, and in a dévissage the original algebra `S` and the stage algebra `A₀` have
independent universes. The proof is the elementary one: the kernel of a surjection of finite
presentation is finitely generated, the kernel of the base change is its image
(`Stacks.Flatness.ker_quotBaseMapₐ`), and the image of a finitely generated ideal is finitely
generated. -/
public theorem finitePresentation_quotBaseMapₐ (f : C →ₐ[R] D) (hsurj : Function.Surjective f)
    (hfp : (f : C →+* D).FinitePresentation) :
    ((quotBaseMapₐ J f : _ →ₐ[R ⧸ J] _) :
      (C ⧸ Ideal.map (algebraMap R C) J) →+*
        (D ⧸ Ideal.map (algebraMap R D) J)).FinitePresentation := by
  have hker : (RingHom.ker (f : C →+* D)).FG := by
    let _ : Algebra C D := (f : C →+* D).toAlgebra
    have _ : Algebra.FinitePresentation C D := hfp
    exact Algebra.FinitePresentation.ker_fG_of_surjective (Algebra.ofId C D) hsurj
  refine RingHom.FinitePresentation.of_surjective _ (quotBaseMapₐ_surjective J f hsurj) ?_
  rw [ker_quotBaseMapₐ J f hsurj]
  exact hker.map _

end Map

/-! ### Finiteness of the quotient base change, and the quotient of the base prime -/

/-- **A finitely generated algebra stays finitely generated after the quotient base change.**
Unlike `RingHom.FiniteType.isStableUnderBaseChange` this is universe-free: `S ⧸ JS` is of finite
type over `R` because it is a quotient of `S`, hence over `R ⧸ J` because that sits in between. -/
public instance finiteTypeQuotBase {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {S : Type*} [CommRing S]
    [Algebra R S] [Algebra.FiniteType R S] (J : Ideal R) :
    Algebra.FiniteType (R ⧸ J) (S ⧸ Ideal.map (algebraMap R S) J) :=
  have _ : Algebra.FiniteType R (S ⧸ Ideal.map (algebraMap R S) J) :=
    Algebra.FiniteType.of_surjective (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ R _) Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  Algebra.FiniteType.of_restrictScalars_finiteType R (R ⧸ J) _

/-- **A finite module stays finite after the quotient base change.** -/
public instance finiteQuotBase {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {S : Type*} [CommRing S] [Algebra R S]
    {N : Type*} [AddCommGroup N] [Module S N] [Module.Finite S N] (J : Ideal R) :
    Module.Finite (S ⧸ Ideal.map (algebraMap R S) J)
      (N ⧸ (Ideal.map (algebraMap R S) J • (⊤ : Submodule S N))) :=
  have _ : Module.Finite S (N ⧸ (Ideal.map (algebraMap R S) J • (⊤ : Submodule S N))) :=
    Module.Finite.of_surjective _ (Submodule.mkQ_surjective _)
  Module.Finite.of_restrictScalars_finite S (S ⧸ Ideal.map (algebraMap R S) J) _

/-- **A prime containing `J` stays prime in `R ⧸ J`.** -/
public theorem isPrime_map_quotient {R : Type*} [CommRing R] (J r : Ideal R) [r.IsPrime]
    (hJ : J ≤ r) : (Ideal.map (algebraMap R (R ⧸ J)) r).IsPrime := by
  rw [Ideal.Quotient.algebraMap_eq]
  exact Ideal.map_isPrime_of_surjective Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective (by rwa [Ideal.mk_ker])

/-- **A finite free module base changes to a finite free module, surjectively.** -/
public theorem mapRange_linearMap_surjective {B B' : Type*} [CommRing B] [CommRing B']
    [Algebra B B'] (hs : Function.Surjective (algebraMap B B')) (ι : Type*) :
    Function.Surjective (Finsupp.mapRange.linearMap (α := ι) (Algebra.linearMap B B')) :=
  Finsupp.mapRange_surjective _ (map_zero _) hs

/-- A `B`-linear surjection `M → M ⧸ JC·M` is a base change along `B → B ⧸ JB`. -/
private theorem isBaseChange_of_mk_smul_top {R C : Type*} {B B' : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing B]
    [CommRing C] [CommRing B'] [Algebra R B] [Algebra R C] [Algebra B C] [IsScalarTower R B C]
    [Algebra B B'] {M : Type w} [AddCommGroup M] [Module C M] [Module B M] [IsScalarTower B C M]
    (J : Ideal R) [Module B' (M ⧸ (Ideal.map (algebraMap R C) J • (⊤ : Submodule C M)))]
    [IsScalarTower B B' (M ⧸ (Ideal.map (algebraMap R C) J • (⊤ : Submodule C M)))]
    (hs : Function.Surjective (algebraMap B B'))
    (hk : RingHom.ker (algebraMap B B') = Ideal.map (algebraMap R B) J)
    (g : M →ₗ[B] M ⧸ (Ideal.map (algebraMap R C) J • (⊤ : Submodule C M)))
    (hg : ∀ x, g x = Submodule.Quotient.mk x) : IsBaseChange B' g := by
  refine isBaseChange_of_surjective hs g (fun y => ?_) fun x hx => ?_
  · obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := Submodule.Quotient.mk_surjective _ y
    exact ⟨x, hg x⟩
  · rw [hk, ← restrictScalars_map_smul_top (B := B) (C := C)]
    exact (Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero _).mp ((hg x).symm.trans (LinearMap.mem_ker.mp hx))

/-- **The quotient of a module by the submodule generated by `J` is its base change.** -/
public theorem isBaseChange_mkQ_smul_top {R : Type*} [CommRing R] (J : Ideal R) (S : Type u)
    [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] (N : Type w) [AddCommGroup N] [Module S N] :
    IsBaseChange (S ⧸ Ideal.map (algebraMap R S) J)
      ((Ideal.map (algebraMap R S) J • (⊤ : Submodule S N)).mkQ) :=
  isBaseChange_of_mk_smul_top (B := S) (C := S) (M := N) J (Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective)
    (Ideal.mk_ker) (Submodule.mkQ _) fun _ => rfl

/-! ### Smoothness and geometrically irreducible fibres -/

/-- **Smoothness of a dévissage stage's lower algebra survives the quotient base change.** The
square of rings is a pushout by `Stacks.FiberCotangentIdentification.isPushout_quotient`, and
smoothness is stable under base change. -/
public theorem smooth_quotBase {R : Type u} [CommRing R] (J : Ideal R) (B : Type u) [CommRing B]
    [Algebra R B] [Algebra.Smooth R B] :
    Algebra.Smooth (R ⧸ J) (B ⧸ Ideal.map (algebraMap R B) J) := by
  have _ : Algebra.IsPushout R B (R ⧸ J) (B ⧸ Ideal.map (algebraMap R B) J) :=
    (Stacks.FiberCotangentIdentification.isPushout_quotient (A := R) (B := B) J).symm
  rw [← RingHom.smooth_algebraMap]
  exact RingHom.Smooth.isStableUnderBaseChange R B (R ⧸ J) (B ⧸ Ideal.map (algebraMap R B) J)
    (RingHom.smooth_algebraMap.mpr ‹_›)

/-- **Geometric irreducibility of the fibres of `Spec(B) → Spec(R)` survives the quotient base
change.** The square of affine schemes is cartesian by
`Stacks.Flatness.isPullback_SpecMap_quotient`, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.GeometricallyIrreducible` is stable under base change. -/
public theorem geometricallyIrreducible_quotBase {R : Type u} [CommRing R] (J : Ideal R)
    (B : Type u) [CommRing B] [Algebra R B]
    [GeometricallyIrreducible (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap R B)))] :
    GeometricallyIrreducible (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
      (algebraMap (R ⧸ J) (B ⧸ Ideal.map (algebraMap R B) J)))) :=
  MorphismProperty.of_isPullback (P := @GeometricallyIrreducible)
    (isPullback_SpecMap_quotient (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap R B)) J) ‹_›

end Stacks.Flatness

namespace Module.CompleteDevissage

variable {R : Type u} {S : Type v} {N : Type w} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [Algebra R S]
  [Algebra.FiniteType R S] [AddCommGroup N] [Module S N] [Module.Finite S N] {r : Ideal R}
  [r.IsPrime] (D : CompleteDevissage R S N r) (J : Ideal R)

/-! ### The quotient stage data -/

/-- The quotient of the upper algebra at stage `i` by the ideal generated by `J`. -/
public abbrev quotA (i : Fin (D.stepCount + 1)) : Type u :=
  D.A i ⧸ Ideal.map (algebraMap R (D.A i)) J

/-- The quotient of the lower algebra at stage `i` by the ideal generated by `J`. -/
public abbrev quotB (i : Fin (D.stepCount + 1)) : Type u :=
  D.B i ⧸ Ideal.map (algebraMap R (D.B i)) J

/-- The quotient of the module at stage `i` by the submodule generated by `J`. -/
public abbrev quotM (i : Fin (D.stepCount + 1)) : Type w :=
  D.M i ⧸ (Ideal.map (algebraMap R (D.A i)) J • (⊤ : Submodule (D.A i) (D.M i)))

/-- The quotient map of the module at stage `i`, as a map of modules over the lower algebra. -/
public def quotMk (i : Fin (D.stepCount + 1)) : D.M i →ₗ[D.B i] D.quotM J i where
  toFun := Submodule.Quotient.mk
  map_add' _ _ := rfl
  map_smul' _ _ := rfl

/-- The quotient base change of the map from the lower to the upper algebra at a stage. -/
public def quotToLeft (i : Fin (D.stepCount + 1)) : D.quotB J i →ₐ[R ⧸ J] D.quotA J i :=
  Stacks.Flatness.quotBaseMapₐ J (D.toLeft i)

/-- The quotient base change of the map from a lower algebra to the next upper algebra. -/
public def quotToRight (i : Fin D.stepCount) : D.quotB J i.castSucc →ₐ[R ⧸ J] D.quotA J i.succ :=
  Stacks.Flatness.quotBaseMapₐ J (D.toRight i)

/-- The quotient lower algebra at a stage acts on the quotient module through the quotient
`toLeft`. -/
public noncomputable instance moduleQuotBQuotM (i : Fin (D.stepCount + 1)) :
    Module (D.quotB J i) (D.quotM J i) :=
  Module.compHom (D.quotM J i) (D.quotToLeft J i).toRingHom

/-- The lower algebra, the quotient lower algebra and the quotient module at a stage form a
scalar tower. -/
public instance isScalarTowerBQuotBQuotM (i : Fin (D.stepCount + 1)) :
    IsScalarTower (D.B i) (D.quotB J i) (D.quotM J i) :=
  IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_smul fun b z => by
    induction z using Submodule.Quotient.induction_on with
    | H x => rfl

/-- The quotient upper algebra at a stage is an algebra over the quotient lower one. -/
public noncomputable instance algebraQuotBQuotA (i : Fin (D.stepCount + 1)) :
    Algebra (D.quotB J i) (D.quotA J i) := (D.quotToLeft J i).toRingHom.toAlgebra

/-- The lower algebra, the quotient lower algebra and the quotient upper algebra at a stage form a
scalar tower. -/
public instance isScalarTowerBQuotBQuotA (i : Fin (D.stepCount + 1)) :
    IsScalarTower (D.B i) (D.quotB J i) (D.quotA J i) :=
  IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_smul fun b z => by
    induction z using Submodule.Quotient.induction_on with
    | H x => rfl

/-- The quotient lower algebra, the quotient upper algebra and the quotient module at a stage form
a scalar tower. -/
public instance isScalarTowerQuotBQuotAQuotM (i : Fin (D.stepCount + 1)) :
    IsScalarTower (D.quotB J i) (D.quotA J i) (D.quotM J i) :=
  ⟨fun b a m => by
    change (D.quotToLeft J i b * a) • m = D.quotToLeft J i b • (a • m)
    rw [mul_smul]⟩

/-- **The quotient module at a stage is the base change of the stage module.** -/
public theorem isBaseChange_quotMk (i : Fin (D.stepCount + 1)) :
    IsBaseChange (D.quotB J i) (D.quotMk J i) :=
  Stacks.Flatness.isBaseChange_of_mk_smul_top (B := D.B i) (C := D.A i) (M := D.M i) J
    Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective Ideal.mk_ker (D.quotMk J i) fun _ => rfl

/-- The quotient base change of the map of a dévissage stage. -/
public noncomputable def quotAlpha (i : Fin (D.stepCount + 1)) :
    (Fin (D.multiplicity i) →₀ D.quotB J i) →ₗ[D.quotB J i] D.quotM J i :=
  (Stacks.Flatness.isBaseChange_finsuppMapRange (D.B i) (D.quotB J i)
    (Fin (D.multiplicity i))).lift ((D.quotMk J i) ∘ₗ D.alpha i)

/-- The quotient map of a stage is the quotient base change of the map of that stage. -/
public theorem quotAlpha_mapRange (i : Fin (D.stepCount + 1))
    (x : Fin (D.multiplicity i) →₀ D.B i) :
    D.quotAlpha J i (Finsupp.mapRange.linearMap (Algebra.linearMap (D.B i) (D.quotB J i)) x)
      = D.quotMk J i (D.alpha i x) :=
  IsBaseChange.lift_eq _ _ x

/-- **The quotient module at a stage is finite over the quotient upper algebra.** -/
public instance finiteQuotAQuotM (i : Fin (D.stepCount + 1)) :
    Module.Finite (D.quotA J i) (D.quotM J i) :=
  have _ : Module.Finite (D.A i) (D.quotM J i) :=
    Module.Finite.of_surjective _ (Submodule.mkQ_surjective _)
  Module.Finite.of_restrictScalars_finite (D.A i) (D.quotA J i) (D.quotM J i)

/-- **The quotient upper algebra at a stage is finite over the quotient lower algebra.** -/
public instance finiteQuotBQuotA (i : Fin (D.stepCount + 1)) :
    Module.Finite (D.quotB J i) (D.quotA J i) :=
  have _ : Module.Finite (D.B i) (D.quotA J i) :=
    Module.Finite.of_surjective
      ({ toFun := Submodule.Quotient.mk, map_add' := fun _ _ => rfl,
          map_smul' := fun _ _ => rfl } : D.A i →ₗ[D.B i] D.quotA J i)
      (Submodule.Quotient.mk_surjective _)
  Module.Finite.of_restrictScalars_finite (D.B i) (D.quotB J i) (D.quotA J i)

/-! ### The quotient transition data -/

/-- A quotient lower algebra acts on the next stage's quotient module through the quotient
`toRight`. -/
public noncomputable instance moduleQuotBQuotMsucc (i : Fin D.stepCount) :
    Module (D.quotB J i.castSucc) (D.quotM J i.succ) :=
  Module.compHom (D.quotM J i.succ) (D.quotToRight J i).toRingHom

/-- The lower algebra and the quotient lower algebra at a stage, and the quotient module of the
next stage, form a scalar tower. -/
public instance isScalarTowerBQuotBQuotMsucc (i : Fin D.stepCount) :
    IsScalarTower (D.B i.castSucc) (D.quotB J i.castSucc) (D.quotM J i.succ) :=
  IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_smul fun b z => by
    induction z using Submodule.Quotient.induction_on with
    | H x => rfl

/-- The quotient map of the next stage's module, as a map of modules over the lower algebra of
the current stage. -/
public def quotMkSucc (i : Fin D.stepCount) : D.M i.succ →ₗ[D.B i.castSucc] D.quotM J i.succ where
  toFun := Submodule.Quotient.mk
  map_add' _ _ := rfl
  map_smul' _ _ := rfl

/-- **The next stage's quotient module is the base change of that stage's module.** -/
public theorem isBaseChange_quotMkSucc (i : Fin D.stepCount) :
    IsBaseChange (D.quotB J i.castSucc) (D.quotMkSucc J i) :=
  Stacks.Flatness.isBaseChange_of_mk_smul_top (B := D.B i.castSucc) (C := D.A i.succ)
    (M := D.M i.succ) J Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective Ideal.mk_ker (D.quotMkSucc J i) fun _ => rfl

/-! ### The quotient cokernel identification -/

/-- The image of the map of a stage lands in the kernel of the quotient of the quotient map. -/
public theorem range_alpha_le_ker_quot (i : Fin (D.stepCount + 1)) :
    LinearMap.range (D.alpha i) ≤ LinearMap.ker
      (((LinearMap.range (D.quotAlpha J i)).mkQ).restrictScalars (D.B i) ∘ₗ D.quotMk J i) := by
  rintro y ⟨x, rfl⟩
  rw [LinearMap.mem_ker]
  show Submodule.Quotient.mk (D.quotMk J i (D.alpha i x)) = 0
  rw [← D.quotAlpha_mapRange J i x]
  exact (Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero _).mpr (LinearMap.mem_range_self _ _)

/-- The map on cokernels induced by the quotient map of a stage. -/
public noncomputable def quotCokerMap (i : Fin (D.stepCount + 1)) :
    (D.M i ⧸ LinearMap.range (D.alpha i)) →ₗ[D.B i]
      (D.quotM J i ⧸ LinearMap.range (D.quotAlpha J i)) :=
  Submodule.liftQ _ _ (D.range_alpha_le_ker_quot J i)

/-- The forward map of the quotient cokernel identification: the base change of the composite
`Mᵢ → Mᵢ ⧸ im αᵢ ≅ Mᵢ₊₁ → Mᵢ₊₁ ⧸ JMᵢ₊₁`. -/
public noncomputable def quotCokerForward (i : Fin D.stepCount) :
    D.quotM J i.castSucc →ₗ[D.quotB J i.castSucc] D.quotM J i.succ :=
  (D.isBaseChange_quotMk J i.castSucc).lift
    ((D.quotMkSucc J i) ∘ₗ (D.cokerEquiv i).toLinearMap ∘ₗ
      (LinearMap.range (D.alpha i.castSucc)).mkQ)

/-- The forward map of the quotient cokernel identification sends the class of `x` to the class
of the image of `x` under `D.cokerEquiv i`. -/
public theorem quotCokerForward_quotMk (i : Fin D.stepCount) (x : D.M i.castSucc) :
    D.quotCokerForward J i (D.quotMk J i.castSucc x)
      = D.quotMkSucc J i (D.cokerEquiv i (Submodule.Quotient.mk x)) :=
  IsBaseChange.lift_eq _ _ x

/-- The backward map of the quotient cokernel identification. -/
public noncomputable def quotCokerBackward (i : Fin D.stepCount) :
    D.quotM J i.succ →ₗ[D.quotB J i.castSucc]
      (D.quotM J i.castSucc ⧸ LinearMap.range (D.quotAlpha J i.castSucc)) :=
  (D.isBaseChange_quotMkSucc J i).lift
    ((D.quotCokerMap J i.castSucc) ∘ₗ (D.cokerEquiv i).symm.toLinearMap)

/-- The backward map of the quotient cokernel identification sends the class of `y` to the image
under `D.quotCokerMap` of `(D.cokerEquiv i).symm y`. -/
public theorem quotCokerBackward_quotMkSucc (i : Fin D.stepCount) (y : D.M i.succ) :
    D.quotCokerBackward J i (D.quotMkSucc J i y)
      = D.quotCokerMap J i.castSucc ((D.cokerEquiv i).symm y) :=
  IsBaseChange.lift_eq _ _ y

/-- The image of the base-changed stage map lands in the kernel of the forward map. -/
public theorem range_quotAlpha_le_ker_forward (i : Fin D.stepCount) :
    LinearMap.range (D.quotAlpha J i.castSucc) ≤ LinearMap.ker (D.quotCokerForward J i) := by
  rintro y ⟨z, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := Stacks.Flatness.mapRange_linearMap_surjective
    (B' := D.quotB J i.castSucc) Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective (Fin (D.multiplicity i.castSucc)) z
  rw [LinearMap.mem_ker, D.quotAlpha_mapRange, D.quotCokerForward_quotMk,
    show (Submodule.Quotient.mk (D.alpha i.castSucc x) :
        D.M i.castSucc ⧸ LinearMap.range (D.alpha i.castSucc)) = 0 from
      (Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero _).mpr (LinearMap.mem_range_self _ x),
    map_zero, map_zero]

/-- The forward map of the quotient cokernel identification, descended to the cokernel. -/
public noncomputable def quotCokerForwardQ (i : Fin D.stepCount) :
    (D.quotM J i.castSucc ⧸ LinearMap.range (D.quotAlpha J i.castSucc)) →ₗ[D.quotB J i.castSucc]
      D.quotM J i.succ :=
  Submodule.liftQ _ (D.quotCokerForward J i) (D.range_quotAlpha_le_ker_forward J i)

/-- `D.quotCokerForwardQ J i` agrees with `D.quotCokerForward J i` on classes. -/
@[simp]
public theorem quotCokerForwardQ_mk (i : Fin D.stepCount) (z : D.quotM J i.castSucc) :
    D.quotCokerForwardQ J i (Submodule.Quotient.mk z) = D.quotCokerForward J i z := rfl

/-- **The cokernel identification of a stage, base changed.** -/
public noncomputable def quotCokerEquiv (i : Fin D.stepCount) :
    (D.quotM J i.castSucc ⧸ LinearMap.range (D.quotAlpha J i.castSucc)) ≃ₗ[D.quotB J i.castSucc]
      D.quotM J i.succ := by
  refine LinearEquiv.ofLinear (D.quotCokerForwardQ J i) (D.quotCokerBackward J i)
    (LinearMap.ext fun z => ?_) (LinearMap.ext fun w => ?_)
  · obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := Submodule.Quotient.mk_surjective _ z
    obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := Submodule.Quotient.mk_surjective
      (LinearMap.range (D.alpha i.castSucc)) ((D.cokerEquiv i).symm y)
    change D.quotCokerForwardQ J i (D.quotCokerBackward J i (D.quotMkSucc J i y)) = _
    rw [D.quotCokerBackward_quotMkSucc, ← hx]
    change D.quotCokerForwardQ J i (Submodule.Quotient.mk (D.quotMk J i.castSucc x)) = _
    rw [D.quotCokerForwardQ_mk, D.quotCokerForward_quotMk, hx, LinearEquiv.apply_symm_apply]
    rfl
  · obtain ⟨z, rfl⟩ := Submodule.Quotient.mk_surjective _ w
    obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := Submodule.Quotient.mk_surjective _ z
    change D.quotCokerBackward J i (D.quotCokerForwardQ J i
      (Submodule.Quotient.mk (D.quotMk J i.castSucc x))) = _
    rw [D.quotCokerForwardQ_mk, D.quotCokerForward_quotMk, D.quotCokerBackward_quotMkSucc,
      LinearEquiv.symm_apply_apply]
    rfl

/-! ### The quotient initial data -/

/-- The quotient base change of the map from the original algebra to the first upper algebra. -/
public def quotToA₀ : (S ⧸ Ideal.map (algebraMap R S) J) →ₐ[R ⧸ J] D.quotA J 0 :=
  Stacks.Flatness.quotBaseMapₐ J D.toA₀

/-- The quotient original algebra acts on the first quotient module through the quotient initial
map. -/
public noncomputable instance moduleQuotSQuotM₀ :
    Module (S ⧸ Ideal.map (algebraMap R S) J) (D.quotM J 0) :=
  Module.compHom (D.quotM J 0) (D.quotToA₀ J).toRingHom

/-- The original algebra, its quotient and the quotient module of the first stage form a scalar
tower. -/
public instance isScalarTowerSQuotSQuotM₀ :
    IsScalarTower S (S ⧸ Ideal.map (algebraMap R S) J) (D.quotM J 0) :=
  IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_smul fun s z => by
    induction z using Submodule.Quotient.induction_on with
    | H x => rfl

/-- The quotient map of the first stage's module, as a map of modules over the original
algebra. -/
public def quotMk₀ : D.M 0 →ₗ[S] D.quotM J 0 where
  toFun := Submodule.Quotient.mk
  map_add' _ _ := rfl
  map_smul' _ _ := rfl

/-- **The first quotient module is the base change of the first stage module.** -/
public theorem isBaseChange_quotMk₀ :
    IsBaseChange (S ⧸ Ideal.map (algebraMap R S) J) (D.quotMk₀ J) :=
  Stacks.Flatness.isBaseChange_of_mk_smul_top (B := S) (C := D.A 0) (M := D.M 0) J
    Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective Ideal.mk_ker (D.quotMk₀ J) fun _ => rfl

/-- The forward map of the base-changed original module identification. -/
public noncomputable def quotInitialForward :
    (N ⧸ (Ideal.map (algebraMap R S) J • (⊤ : Submodule S N)))
      →ₗ[S ⧸ Ideal.map (algebraMap R S) J] D.quotM J 0 :=
  (Stacks.Flatness.isBaseChange_mkQ_smul_top J S N).lift
    ((D.quotMk₀ J) ∘ₗ D.initialEquiv.toLinearMap)

/-- The forward map of the base-changed original module identification sends the class of `n` to
the class of `D.initialEquiv n`. -/
public theorem quotInitialForward_mk (n : N) :
    D.quotInitialForward J (Submodule.Quotient.mk n) = D.quotMk₀ J (D.initialEquiv n) :=
  IsBaseChange.lift_eq _ _ n

/-- The backward map of the base-changed original module identification. -/
public noncomputable def quotInitialBackward :
    D.quotM J 0 →ₗ[S ⧸ Ideal.map (algebraMap R S) J]
      (N ⧸ (Ideal.map (algebraMap R S) J • (⊤ : Submodule S N))) :=
  (D.isBaseChange_quotMk₀ J).lift
    ((Ideal.map (algebraMap R S) J • (⊤ : Submodule S N)).mkQ ∘ₗ
      D.initialEquiv.symm.toLinearMap)

/-- The backward map of the base-changed original module identification sends the class of `x` to
the class of `D.initialEquiv.symm x`. -/
public theorem quotInitialBackward_quotMk₀ (x : D.M 0) :
    D.quotInitialBackward J (D.quotMk₀ J x) = Submodule.Quotient.mk (D.initialEquiv.symm x) :=
  IsBaseChange.lift_eq _ _ x

/-- **The original module identification, base changed.** -/
public noncomputable def quotInitialEquiv :
    (N ⧸ (Ideal.map (algebraMap R S) J • (⊤ : Submodule S N)))
      ≃ₗ[S ⧸ Ideal.map (algebraMap R S) J] D.quotM J 0 := by
  refine LinearEquiv.ofLinear (D.quotInitialForward J) (D.quotInitialBackward J)
    (LinearMap.ext fun z => ?_) (LinearMap.ext fun w => ?_)
  · obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := Submodule.Quotient.mk_surjective _ z
    change D.quotInitialForward J (D.quotInitialBackward J (D.quotMk₀ J x)) = _
    rw [D.quotInitialBackward_quotMk₀, D.quotInitialForward_mk, LinearEquiv.apply_symm_apply]
    rfl
  · obtain ⟨n, rfl⟩ := Submodule.Quotient.mk_surjective _ w
    change D.quotInitialBackward J (D.quotInitialForward J (Submodule.Quotient.mk n)) = _
    rw [D.quotInitialForward_mk, D.quotInitialBackward_quotMk₀, LinearEquiv.symm_apply_apply]
    rfl

/-! ### The fibre prime of the base-changed stage -/

/-- **The kernel of `Bᵢ → Bᵢ ⧸ JBᵢ` lies inside the fibre prime `rBᵢ`**, because `J ⊆ r`. -/
public theorem ker_quotB_le (hJ : J ≤ r) (i : Fin (D.stepCount + 1)) :
    RingHom.ker (algebraMap (D.B i) (D.quotB J i)) ≤ Ideal.map (algebraMap R (D.B i)) r :=
  le_trans (le_of_eq (show RingHom.ker (algebraMap (D.B i) (D.quotB J i))
    = Ideal.map (algebraMap R (D.B i)) J from Ideal.mk_ker)) (Ideal.map_mono hJ)

/-- **The fibre prime of the base-changed stage is prime.** -/
public theorem isPrime_map_quotB (hJ : J ≤ r)
    [(Ideal.map (algebraMap R (R ⧸ J)) r).IsPrime] (i : Fin (D.stepCount + 1)) :
    (Ideal.map (algebraMap (R ⧸ J) (D.quotB J i))
      (Ideal.map (algebraMap R (R ⧸ J)) r)).IsPrime :=
  Stacks.Flatness.isPrime_map_algebraMap_of_surjective r (R ⧸ J) (D.quotB J i)
    Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective (D.ker_quotB_le J hJ i)

/-- **The fibre prime of the base-changed stage contracts to the old fibre prime.** -/
public theorem map_quotB_eq_comap (hJ : J ≤ r) (i : Fin (D.stepCount + 1)) :
    Ideal.map (algebraMap R (D.B i)) r
      = (Ideal.map (algebraMap (R ⧸ J) (D.quotB J i))
          (Ideal.map (algebraMap R (R ⧸ J)) r)).comap (algebraMap (D.B i) (D.quotB J i)) :=
  Stacks.Flatness.map_algebraMap_eq_comap_of_surjective r (R ⧸ J) (D.quotB J i)
    Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective (D.ker_quotB_le J hJ i)

/-! ### The base change of the dévissage -/

/-- **The base change of a complete dévissage along a surjection of the base.**

Given a complete dévissage of `N/S/R` over a prime `r` of `R` (Stacks 05HX) and an ideal
`J ⊆ r`, quotienting every ring and every module by the ideal and submodule generated by `J`
gives a complete dévissage of `(N/JN)/(S/JS)/(R/J)` over `r/J`. This is the base change Stacks
05PG's induction step performs when it replaces `A` by `A/J`.

Every condition is one of the lemmas of this file and of
`StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Flat.DevissageQuotientBase`; the only non-instance input is `J ⊆ r`,
which is what makes the fibre prime `rBᵢ` contain `JBᵢ` and so survive the quotient. -/
public noncomputable def quotientBase (hJ : J ≤ r)
    [(Ideal.map (algebraMap R (R ⧸ J)) r).IsPrime] :
    CompleteDevissage (R ⧸ J) (S ⧸ Ideal.map (algebraMap R S) J)
      (N ⧸ (Ideal.map (algebraMap R S) J • (⊤ : Submodule S N)))
      (Ideal.map (algebraMap R (R ⧸ J)) r) where
  stepCount := D.stepCount
  A := D.quotA J
  B := D.quotB J
  M := D.quotM J
  toA₀ := D.quotToA₀ J
  toLeft := D.quotToLeft J
  toRight := D.quotToRight J
  multiplicity := D.multiplicity
  alpha := D.quotAlpha J
  finiteM i := D.finiteQuotAQuotM J i
  initial_surjective :=
    Stacks.Flatness.quotBaseMapₐ_surjective J D.toA₀ D.initial_surjective
  initial_finitePresentation :=
    Stacks.Flatness.finitePresentation_quotBaseMapₐ J D.toA₀ D.initial_surjective
      D.initial_finitePresentation
  transition_surjective i :=
    Stacks.Flatness.quotBaseMapₐ_surjective J (D.toRight i) (D.transition_surjective i)
  transition_finitePresentation i :=
    Stacks.Flatness.finitePresentation_quotBaseMapₐ J (D.toRight i) (D.transition_surjective i)
      (D.transition_finitePresentation i)
  left_finite i := RingHom.finite_algebraMap.mpr (D.finiteQuotBQuotA J i)
  smooth i := Stacks.Flatness.smooth_quotBase J (D.B i)
  geometricallyIrreducibleFibers i := Stacks.Flatness.geometricallyIrreducible_quotBase J (D.B i)
  initialEquiv := D.quotInitialEquiv J
  cokerEquiv := D.quotCokerEquiv J
  map_isPrime i := D.isPrime_map_quotB J hJ i
  fiber_bijective i :=
    haveI := D.isPrime_map_quotB J hJ i
    Stacks.Flatness.fiber_bijective_of_isBaseChange (D.alpha i)
      (D.isBaseChange_quotMk J i) (D.quotAlpha J i) (D.quotAlpha_mapRange J i)
      (Ideal.map (algebraMap R (D.B i)) r)
      (Ideal.map (algebraMap (R ⧸ J) (D.quotB J i)) (Ideal.map (algebraMap R (R ⧸ J)) r))
      (D.map_quotB_eq_comap J hJ i)
      (Stacks.Flatness.bijective_residueFieldMap_of_surjective Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective _ _ _)
      (D.fiber_bijective i)
  final_surjective := by
    change Function.Surjective (D.quotAlpha J (Fin.last D.stepCount))
    intro z
    obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := Submodule.Quotient.mk_surjective _ z
    obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := D.final_surjective y
    refine ⟨Finsupp.mapRange.linearMap
      (Algebra.linearMap (D.B (Fin.last D.stepCount)) (D.quotB J (Fin.last D.stepCount))) x, ?_⟩
    rw [D.quotAlpha_mapRange, hx]
    rfl

/-- The quotient dévissage has as many steps as `D`. -/
@[simp]
public theorem stepCount_quotientBase (hJ : J ≤ r)
    [(Ideal.map (algebraMap R (R ⧸ J)) r).IsPrime] :
    (D.quotientBase J hJ).stepCount = D.stepCount := rfl

end Module.CompleteDevissage

end
